Package: bayesintervals
Title: Reducible Imprecision and Bayesian Intervals for Mixed Models
Version: 3.0.0
Authors@R:
    c(person("Ekin", "Ören", , "ekin.oren.3@gmail.com", role = c("aut", "cre")),
      person("Sebastian", "Schmitz", role = "aut"),
      person("Sanofi", role = c("cph", "fnd")))
Description: Calculates and visualizes Bayesian credible, prediction and
    tolerance intervals, and posterior predictive distributions, for linear
    mixed models from Markov chain Monte Carlo (MCMC) samples of the model
    parameters. Users define the model through fixed effects, variance
    components and optional covariates, and results can be back-transformed
    from the log scale. Tolerance intervals are derived from the posterior
    predictive distribution following Krishnamoorthy and Mathew (2009)
    <doi:10.1002/9780470473900>, including the construction of one-dimensional
    two-sided intervals from the bivariate posterior of the lower and upper
    quantiles. Reducible imprecision measures the share of the
    tolerance-interval half-width that exceeds the prediction-interval
    half-width, that is, the epistemic uncertainty that more data could
    reduce. The package includes an interactive 'shiny' application, started
    with start_app_view(), which has its own name: 'BSI' (Bayesian
    Statistical Intervals). The development repository on 'GitHub' is called
    'BayesianSI.Calculator'.
